    "explanation": "'By the time the guests arrive, you'll have already made dinner': Quando gli ospiti arriveranno, tu avrai già preparato la cena. The completed-before-a-future-point action takes the futuro anteriore: the future of avere (avrai) plus the participle preparato. The simple future preparerai would just say 'you will prepare'. With avere the participle is invariable (not preparata).",
