    ],
    "explanation": "'By the time you arrive, Marco will have already left': Quando arriverai, Marco sarà già partito. The futuro anteriore of partire uses essere (a motion verb): the future of essere (sarà) plus the participle. With essere the participle agrees with the subject, and Marco is masculine singular, so it is partito. Using avere (avrà) would be the wrong auxiliary.",
    "examiner_note": "Two markpoints: future-auxiliary formation (this tree) and participle agreement masculine singular (PP tree). Full answer 'sarà partito'.",
